# The First Noel, melody with chords (repertoire plan: the-first-noel). A new arrangement of the
# traditional English carol: verse 1 and the refrain, with the tune as it is commonly sung today
# (older printings vary), exactly as independent recollections agreed on it note for note. It is
# played an octave below the sung pitch so the whole tune sits in first position on strings 4, 3
# and 2: D (open string 4), E (string 4 fret 2), F# (string 4 fret 4), G (open string 3),
# A (string 3 fret 2), B (open string 2), C# (string 2 fret 2), D (string 2 fret 3). One finger per
# fret: the fret number is the finger.
# The tune is built from one phrase used again and again. The verse is a single eight-bar line
# sung twice (bars 1-8 and 9-16, the same notes). The refrain (bars 17-24) opens with the verse's
# opening figure, "F# E | D. E F# G | A", and its last four bars are the verse's last four bars,
# note for note. Each time a line comes round, its chords come round with it.
# Chords D (xx0232), G (320003) and A (x02220), one per bar, every one under a melody note it
# contains on beat 1. The teacher strums the open chords on every beat, beat 1 the strongest.
# Then swap parts: strum the chords while the app plays the tune.
title: The First Noel
